{
  "schema_version": "1.1",
  "title": "Manual entity-extraction gold (Mirathorn M1 vertical slice sources)",
  "purpose": "Human-authored expected entities plus temporal provenance targets so LLM ingest can be scored against narrative-state needs (session ordering, OBSERVED vs planning). Pair with evidence units and fact_extractor inheritance rules; not fully wired into CI yet.",
  "aligned_manifest": "evals/llm_ingestion_slice/slice_manifest.json",
  "corpus_gaps": [
    "event_sourced_slice seeds evu_campaign_live_arrival and evu_campaign_live_guard anchor on Session 6 / Miraholm language that does not appear in Longmont Campaign General Notes.md; the deterministic slice uses fallback_text for those units. Full-ingest validation should use Session recap files under Session Recaps/ for live-session entities (e.g. Captain Lysandra at the gate).",
    "Longmont Campaign General Notes.md frontmatter has session: null and source_class: ledger_or_dossier while the deterministic benchmark seeds use inferred_session=6 and planning_document / observed_session_recap. Until recap files (or frontmatter/session splits) populate evidence.document_session or inferred_session per chunk, facts from a raw ingest of General Notes alone will often have asserted_in_session null and will not reproduce Gate D narrative ordering benchmarks."
  ],
  "temporal_provenance": {
    "fact_extractor_source": "src/ingestion/fact_extractor.py::_build_fact_record",
    "inheritance": {
      "asserted_in_session": "evidence.document_session if not null else evidence.inferred_session (coerced to int or null)",
      "sequence_index_within_session": "evidence.source_order_index (global chunk order index for that ingest; deterministic slice fixes six units with indices 0–5)"
    },
    "reducer_projection": "src/reducer/canon_projection.py uses fact.asserted_in_session and fact.sequence_index_within_session when ordering OBSERVED / competing campaign facts—without these fields narrative 'what changed when' cannot be recovered from facts alone.",
    "ingest_gates": "CLI ingest runs gate stage_campaign_narrative_temporal_tick (src/contracts/temporal_tick_gate.py); evals/llm_ingestion_slice runs Gate T - narrative temporal tick. Any fact whose evidence_ids include campaign-layer evidence must have asserted_in_session and/or sequence_index_within_session non-null.",
